# 逆転裁判4 (Gyakuten Saiban 4, AGCJ): the game's own numbers for its characters, as the script has them (16-bit,
# the low byte first, so 0x0090 is written 9000). Read from the card's font (fonts.imb in its file system: 1,840
# glyphs of 16x16, four 4-bit tiles each, in code order from 0x90). Signs, letters and kana were read off numbered
# sheets by one reader; the kanji by manga-ocr glyph by glyph and by the same reader on sheets of each glyph beside
# its reading, 377 of the OCR's readings corrected there, and every correction checked again beside its glyph. The
# whole script (mes_all.bin) was then read through in sentences with the table, and characters given to two
# glyphs were settled by the words they stand in. 0x01A0 is the long-vowel mark, which looks like 一 (0x0228):
# what comes before each tells them apart (katakana before 0x01A0 2,801 times in 3,402). Empty glyphs and the
# game's own icons are left out.
